# Recommended Cybersecurity Practices

## 1. Use Strong Passwords
Create passwords that are difficult to guess. Avoid using personal information and do not share passwords with others.

## 2. Enable Two-Factor Authentication
Use two-factor authentication to add an extra layer of protection to your online accounts.

## 3. Avoid Suspicious Links
Do not open unknown links or attachments from suspicious emails and messages.

## 4. Update Software Regularly
Keep your applications, operating systems and antivirus software updated to fix security weaknesses.

## 5. Back Up Important Data
Keep copies of important files so that they can be recovered if data is lost or damaged.

## Conclusion
Following these practices helps reduce cybersecurity risks and keeps personal information safer.